--- !u!114 &1231388854
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1231388851}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ce99abd7e1ae48a42be8118b7db931af, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueEditor
  dialoguePav:
    name: Dr. Pav
    sentences:
    - what do you think Timmy?
    - "I\u2019m afraid so. Based on what I\u2019m seeing here, you have diabetes,
      Timmy. "
    - "I\u2019m afraid it doesn\u2019t work like that."
    - Well that is one type of diabetes. What you have is type-1 diabetes. While
      some people develop diabetes as a result of their lifestyle, others are simply
      born with it.
    - "Absolutely not. Diabetes is not a death sentence or what makes you, you. It\u2019s
      just an adjustment you need to be conscious of."
    - The feeling of being aware. Having an active lifestyle, eating the right nutritious
      food, and regularly checking your insulin levels.
    - Maybe try it grilled or baked.
    - You can eat candy, but it must be very infrequently, and must be measured.
    - Not all necessarily; but they all need to be looked after and eaten in moderation.
    - "Here, let me print out a list. Why don\u2019t you and your mom head down to
      the cafeteria? We have a wide selection for you to look at."
    - Yes?
    - "Well, it\u2019s not kids LIKE you. You\u2019re just like every kid Timmy,
      and everyone works through life differently. You just gotta move with the curveballs
      you\u2019re thrown."
    - "It WILL feel like that. But remember, You\u2019re still the same soccer pro
      Timmy. Just with a better insight on yourself and how to manage."
    - "Your immune system has already destroyed the beta-cells that makes insulin
      in your pancreas. It\u2019ll be something that you\u2019ll need to consider
      the rest of your life."
    - Let me administer some Insulin for now to make you feel better. It will just
      be another small prick on the arm.
    profile: {fileID: -625310335, guid: 9a8bf3aa13c73474a9b0d3d61d84312e, type: 3}
  dialogueKid:
    name: Timmy
    sentences:
    - "That\u2019s happening inside me???"
    - Well how do we fix this?? Can you give me a few insulin pills or something?
    - "How can this happen? My gran-pa, he has diabetes, but that\u2019s cause mom
      says he eats and sits too much."
    - Am I different from the others Doc? Am I gonna have to quit soccer?
    - Well what is the right food? Cause tonight was gonna fried chicken night-
    - No fried chicken? What about peanut butter cups?
    - Hot dogs? Hamburgers? Bacon??
    - Well Doc, what can I eat?
    - Well, well alright. Doctor Pav?
    - How do kids like me live with this?
    - "Well it feels like I\u2019m being struck out\u2026"
    - "Well alright\u2026 Donuts?"
    - Ok.. well how long do I gotta deal with this til we can fix it?
    - "\u2026lame."
    - Ughh! More Needles?!
    profile: {fileID: -1908978240, guid: 803a7dc6b3c2f8649a12941a58d5884c, type: 3}
  dialogueParent:
    name: 
    sentences: []
    profile: {fileID: 0}
